# Veripsa P0 graph-integrity gate (auto-discovered by run_gates.sh).
# Dedicated extraction passes must never turn bounded/failed evidence into Clear.
register_gate "tests/test_pass_incomplete_diagnostics.py" "PASS DIAGNOSTICS GATE: PASS" "dedicated-pass completeness diagnostics" "Every bounded never-crash graph producer preserves its historical two-value return API while surfacing read/truncation, parse/wrapper failure, and output/work-cap losses as path-local incomplete evidence. The focused fixtures cover a real >1 MiB truncation, config catalog cap propagation, forced wrapper failure, OpenAPI/Kubernetes markers beyond the cap, route probe/pair ceilings, and route scanning over only the caller's .gitattributes-filtered source universe. Normal fixtures remain complete with an empty diagnostics set." "No extraction substrate may silently convert missing graph evidence into Clear; guard-excluded files remain excluded, affected candidate consumers become Unknown, and ordinary inputs remain normal" 30
